---
import PolicyPage from '../components/PolicyPage.astro';
const labels = [
  ['Verified information', 'Facts traceable to a named source and reporting period.'],
  ['Analytical interpretation', 'Native Media’s reading of the evidence, marked as analysis.'],
  ['External projection', 'Forecasts from identified third parties, attributed and never presented as our own.'],
  ['Opinion', 'Views and commentary, always labelled as such.'],
] as const;
const sections = [['what', 'What research means here'], ['featured', 'Research from other organizations'], ['labels', 'Fact, analysis, projection and opinion'], ['data', 'Data and charts'], ['limits', 'What we do not claim'], ['sample', 'Sample data'], ['corrections', 'Corrections']].map(([id, title]) => ({ id, title }));
---
<PolicyPage title="Research Policy" lede="How Native Media chooses, credits and presents research and information." sections={sections}>
  <h2 id="what">What research means here</h2>
  <p>At Native Media, research means collecting, organizing, analyzing and presenting relevant information to support understanding, informed decisions and strategic communication. It is based on credible, published sources.</p>
  <h2 id="featured">Research from other organizations</h2>
  <p>Our Research &amp; Publications section features reports and research written by other organizations. We credit the authors and publisher, link to the original, feature work only with permission, and do not change an author’s figures or conclusions. Featuring a publication is not an endorsement. See <a href="/research-and-publications/third-party-research">how we feature research</a>.</p>
  <h2 id="labels">Fact, analysis, projection and opinion</h2>
  <p>We keep these apart and label them:</p>
  <ul>{labels.map(([t, d]) => <li><strong>{t}.</strong> {d}</li>)}</ul>
  <h2 id="data">Data and charts</h2>
  <p>Every chart and data exhibit shows its title, indicator, reporting period, source, units and any explanatory notes. Charts have a text alternative and a data table.</p>
  <h2 id="limits">What we do not claim</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Native Media does not claim confidential intelligence capabilities, government intelligence affiliations or privileged access.</li>
    <li>We do not promise predictive accuracy or guaranteed decision outcomes.</li>
    <li>We state the limitations of each analysis.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2 id="sample">Sample data</h2>
  <p>Where we build prototypes, any sample data is clearly marked as illustrative and is never presented as fact.</p>
  <h2 id="corrections">Corrections</h2>
  <p>Errors are corrected openly. See the <a href="/editorial-policy#corrections">Editorial Policy</a>.</p>
</PolicyPage>
